# Ignore rules for cli/Dockerfile only.
#
# The build context is the repo root, so a plain `.dockerignore` there would
# apply to every Dockerfile in the tree (deploy/docker/*, .thunderbot). BuildKit
# reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context's, which scopes
# these rules to this image.
#
# Without this, `COPY cli/ ./cli/` overlays the host's `cli/node_modules` on top
# of the frozen install from the layer above. Several dependencies ship
# platform-specific binaries, so a macOS tree landing in a linux image is a
# broken agent that built cleanly.
**/node_modules

# Never let a local credential or build output into an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/auth.json
**/*.key
dist
dist-ssr
dist-isolation
target
.git
